{"id":"u-4d4b2fd5-fe64-4f96-9be3-daf48708e8a4","src":"community","title":"MuscleTruth Hypertrophy Program","author":"Nas N.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/Pk133D-muscletruth-hypertrophy-program","desc":"By only completing two sets per workout with max effort for every set, you provide your body with the stimulus need to incentivize strength gains while simultaneously developing muscle size. Every workout starts with compound based movements to emphasize the targeted muscles for the entire workout and then transitions to isolation work for each dedicated muscle to allow maximum stimulus achieved without excessive bias on a singular muscle.\n\nWorkout is started with push for chest, front deltoids, side deltoids, and triceps, followed by pull for upper back, lats, biceps, and forearms, and finally leg/core day for quads, hamstrings, glutes, calves, and abs.\n\nEach workout features 6 workouts with 2 sets for all but two movements which are the lateral raise and dragon flags. These movements feature 3 sets as I don’t perform maximum intensity on these specific movements but prefer to stop one rep short of true failure in which 3 sets is more appropriate. \n\nThis brings total sets preformed to 13 on push day, 12 on pull day, and 13 on leg/core day. \n\nThis number of sets is more than sufficient volume when the goal is training 4/5 days a week.\n\nAn example 2 weeks following this split would look like\n\nMonday - Push\nTuesday - Pull\nWednesday - Legs/Core\nThursday - Active Rest Day\nFriday - Push\nSaturday - Pull\nSunday - Legs/Core\nMonday - Active Rest Day\n\nTuesday - Push\nWednesday - Pull\nThursday - Legs\nFriday - Active Rest Day\nSaturday - Push\nSunday - Pull\nMonday - Legs/Core\nTuesday - Active Rest Day\n\nThe beauty of this split is its flexibility. If you have to take a day off or multiple, you can just pick up where you left off without worrying about having to skip a workout. As long as you keep following the order of the workouts and resting after 3 days in a row if all consecutive workouts are completed, you can continue to keep making progress throughout the 12 weeks of the program and complete it in its entirety at your preferred rate of advancement.\n\nThe goal of this split is to continue to increase strength while building muscle. You should start by performing each workout in the rep range of 5-12. Certain movements work better in the lower ranges of 5-8 and others might thrive in the 8-12 range. The importance is to achieve true muscular failure for the 2 sets that are allotted to each workout. As stated earlier, I’ve programmed the lateral raises and dragon flags to be performed at 1 rep prior to failure, so 3 sets are provided for those. \n\nEach workout, you should be looking to add one additional rep to the workout you previously did. For example, if last week you performed 6 reps at 185 on the incline smith press to all out failure, the next week you should aim to perform 7 reps with the same weight. Then, when you reach the upper end of your preferred rep range (i.e. 8), you would increase the weight performed by 5 pounds if your smallest available plate is 2.5lbs and then aim for the lower end of your rep range (i.e. 5)\n\nDeload at end of 12 weeks","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-31T03:08:22.606Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["LVHI Push Day","LVHI Pull Day","LVHI Leg/Core Day"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":10},{"r":5,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":10},{"r":7,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":10},{"r":5,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":10},{"r":9,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"r":11,"rpe":10},{"r":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9.5},{"r":11,"rpe":9.5},{"r":10,"rpe":9.5}]}]},{"ex":